    "result": "Excellent! All tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n### 1. **Governance module test** (`src/finetune/governance.test.js`)\n**Problem**: `APPROVAL_STATUSES` couldn't be imported as a named export from the module.\n\n**Fix**: Added named exports in `src/finetune/index.js` for the constants that were previously only available through the default export:\n```javascript\nexport {\n  APPROVAL_STATUSES,\n  DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS,\n  GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS,\n  RISK_LEVELS\n};\n```\n\n### 2. **Toxicity metric test** (`src/eval/index.test.js`)\n**Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` function had a signature mismatch. It expected `(outputs, bannedTerms)` but `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`, causing references to be misinterpreted as banned terms.\n\n**Fix**: Updated the function signature in `src/eval/metrics.js`:\n```javascript\nexport function toxicityMetric(outputs, references, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)\n```\nAdded a safety check to use the default banned terms if the third parameter isn't an array.\n\n## Test Results\n\u2705 All 28 tests passing across 8 test files\n- No test files were modified\n- All existing public exports remain working",
